repomix.files:
This section contains the contents of the repository's files.# This gate executes repository code in a disposable, read-only-token runner.
# It is independent of Friday's metadata-only PR lifecycle workflow.
name: Build identity and determinism gate
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: build-identity-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  identity:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 15
    steps:
      - name: Checkout exact commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Set up Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '22'
          cache: npm
      - name: Install locked dependencies
        run: npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
      - name: Verify committed ruleset and causal tripwire
        run: node tools/ruleset/build-ruleset.mjs --check
      - name: Verify exact build identity against fresh source
        run: node tools/ruleset/build-ruleset.mjs --check-identity
      - name: Verify full determinism suite including identity negatives
        run: npm test -- --runInBand tests/determinism
      - name: Reject accidental historical replay fixture overwrite
        run: npm test -- --runInBand tests/conformance
      - name: Verify production build
        run: npm run build# Optional repo-level GitHub Action. Copy verbatim to .github/workflows/.
# Uses GITHUB_TOKEN and GitHub metadata only. No checkout; never executes PR code.
name: Friday PR lifecycle
on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, reopened, synchronize, edited, ready_for_review, converted_to_draft, closed]
permissions:
  contents: read
  issues: write
  pull-requests: write
jobs:
  lifecycle:
    # We never grant issue-write rights based on a fork-supplied PR body.
    if: github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/github-script@v7
        with:
          script: |
            const {owner, repo} = context.repo;
            const pr = context.payload.pull_request;
            const event = context.payload.action;
            const body = pr.body || '';
            const marker = /<!--\s*friday-issue:\s*(\d+)\s*-->/i.exec(body);
            if (!marker) { core.info('Not a Friday-managed PR; skip'); return; }
            const issue_number = Number(marker[1]);
            if (!Number.isSafeInteger(issue_number) || issue_number < 1) { core.setFailed('Invalid Friday issue marker'); return; }
            const markerScopes = text => {
              const m = /<!--\s*friday-scope:\s*([\s\S]*?)\s*-->/i.exec(text || '');
              return m ? m[1].split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : [];
            };
            const scoped = (scope, file) => scope === file || (scope.endsWith('/**') &&
              (file === scope.slice(0, -3) || file.startsWith(scope.slice(0, -3) + '/')));
            const overlaps = (a, b) => scoped(a,b) || scoped(b,a);
            const labels = {work: 'friday:in-progress', review: 'friday:in-review', done: 'friday:done', todo: 'friday:todo'};
            for (const [key, label] of Object.entries(labels)) {
              try {
                await github.rest.issues.createLabel({owner, repo, name: label,
                  color: {work:'FBCA04',review:'1D76DB',done:'0E8A16',todo:'D4C5F9'}[key],
                  description: 'Friday orchestration lifecycle state'});
              } catch (e) { if (e.status !== 422) throw e; }
            }
            const replaceState = async desired => {
              const issue = await github.rest.issues.get({owner, repo, issue_number});
              if (issue.data.pull_request) { core.setFailed('Marker points to a PR, not an issue'); return; }
              const active = Object.values(labels).filter(label =>
                (issue.data.labels || []).some(l => (typeof l === 'string' ? l : l.name) === label));
              const remove = active.filter(label => label !== desired);
              for (const label of remove) {
                try { await github.rest.issues.removeLabel({owner, repo, issue_number, name: label}); }
                catch (e) { if (e.status !== 404) throw e; }
              }
              if (!active.includes(desired)) await github.rest.issues.addLabels({owner, repo, issue_number, labels: [desired]});
            };
            if (event === 'closed') {
              if (pr.merged) {
                // A stacked PR merged into another feature branch is not yet landed on default.
                const metadata = await github.rest.repos.get({owner, repo});
                const onDefault = pr.base.ref === metadata.data.default_branch;
                if (onDefault) {
                  await replaceState(labels.done);
                  // GitHub auto-closes 'Closes #N' on default; reconcile even if marker-only.
                  await github.rest.issues.update({owner, repo, issue_number, state: 'closed'});
                } else {
                  await replaceState(labels.review);
                }
              } else {
                // Do not free an issue owned by another still-open PR.
                const others = await github.paginate(github.rest.pulls.list, {owner,repo,state:'open',per_page:100});
                const hasReplacement = others.some(p => p.number !== pr.number &&
                  new RegExp('<!--\\s*friday-issue:\\s*' + issue_number + '\\s*-->', 'i').test(p.body || ''));
                if (!hasReplacement) await replaceState(labels.todo);
              }
              return;
            }
            if (!pr.draft) {
              const allFiles = await github.paginate(github.rest.pulls.listFiles,
                {owner,repo,pull_number:pr.number,per_page:100});
              const starter = allFiles.find(f => /^\.friday\/issue-\d+-start\.md$/.test(f.filename));
              if (starter) {
                await replaceState(labels.work);
                core.setFailed('Remove the temporary ' + starter.filename + ' before review');
                return;
              }
            }
            await replaceState(pr.draft ? labels.work : labels.review);
            // Compare actual modified files and declared scopes across different issues.
            // Ignore temporary bootstrap files and report rather than blocking unrelated work.
            const myFiles = (await github.paginate(github.rest.pulls.listFiles,
              {owner,repo,pull_number:pr.number,per_page:100}))
              .map(f=>f.filename).filter(f=>!f.startsWith('.friday/'));
            const myScopes = markerScopes(body);
            const open = await github.paginate(github.rest.pulls.list,{owner,repo,state:'open',per_page:100});
            const conflicts = [];
            for (const other of open) {
              if (other.number === pr.number) continue;
              const theirs = markerScopes(other.body);
              const fileHits = (myFiles.length || myScopes.length)
                ? (await github.paginate(github.rest.pulls.listFiles,
                   {owner,repo,pull_number:other.number,per_page:100})).map(f=>f.filename).filter(f=>!f.startsWith('.friday/')) : [];
              const hits = new Set();
              for (const f of myFiles) {
                if (fileHits.includes(f) || theirs.some(s=>scoped(s,f))) hits.add(f);
              }
              for (const s of myScopes) {
                for (const t of theirs) if (overlaps(s,t)) hits.add(s+' ↔ '+t);
                for (const f of fileHits) if (scoped(s,f)) hits.add(s+' ↔ '+f);
              }
              if (hits.size) conflicts.push({number:other.number, hits:[...hits].slice(0,12)});
            }
            const signature = '<!-- friday-overlap-report -->';
            const report = signature + '\n### Friday cross-PR overlap scan\n\n' +
              (conflicts.length ? conflicts.map(c => `- PR #${c.number}: ${c.hits.map(s=>'\x60'+s+'\x60').join(', ')}`).join('\n') :
                'No overlapping declared scopes or changed files detected among currently open PRs.') +
              '\n\n*This is an advisory scan of declared scopes and committed PR changes, not uncommitted work. Coordinate overlapping changes before merging.*';
            const comments = await github.paginate(github.rest.issues.listComments,
              {owner,repo,issue_number:pr.number,per_page:100});
            const prior = comments.find(c=>c.user?.type === 'Bot' && c.body?.includes(signature));
            if (prior) {
              if (prior.body !== report) await github.rest.issues.updateComment({owner,repo,comment_id:prior.id,body:report});
            } else if (conflicts.length || myScopes.length) {
              await github.rest.issues.createComment({owner,repo,issue_number:pr.number,body:report});
            }name: Deploy GitHub Pages
on:
  pull_request:
    paths:
      - '.github/workflows/pages.yml'
      - 'tools/hosting-browser-smoke.mjs'
      - 'src/**'
      - 'public/**'
      - '*.html'
      - 'vite.config.js'
      - 'package*.json'
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: read
concurrency:
  group: pages-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: false
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 20
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '22'
          cache: npm
      - uses: actions/configure-pages@v5
        id: pages
        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'
      - name: Select base path
        id: base
        env:
          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}
          REPO_NAME: ${{ github.event.repository.name }}
          PAGES_BASE: ${{ steps.pages.outputs.base_path }}
        run: |
          if [ "$EVENT" = pull_request ]; then PAGES_BASE="/$REPO_NAME"; fi
          echo "path=${PAGES_BASE%/}/" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
      - run: npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
        env:
          PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD: '1'
      - run: npm test -- --runInBand tests/src/pwa-install-shell.test.js tests/src/music-pack.test.js tests/src/continuous-soundtrack-menu-shuffle.test.js
      - name: Build for Pages base path
        env:
          BASE: ${{ steps.base.outputs.path }}
        run: npm run build -- --base "$BASE"
      - name: Install Chromium
        run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium
      - name: Smoke test production game
        env:
          BASE: ${{ steps.base.outputs.path }}
        run: |
          npm run preview -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4173 --strictPort --base "$BASE" > /tmp/pages-preview.log 2>&1 &
          server=$!
          trap 'kill "$server" 2>/dev/null || true' EXIT
          for i in $(seq 1 30); do curl -fsS "http://127.0.0.1:4173$BASE" >/dev/null && break; sleep 1; done
          node tools/hosting-browser-smoke.mjs "http://127.0.0.1:4173$BASE"
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
        with:
          path: dist
  deploy:
    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
    needs: build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      pages: write
      id-token: write
    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
        id: deployment# Issue #211 — gameplay-input reachability matrix

Bounded leaf: **verify current reachability and prove/disprove one suspected alias defect**. This is
*not* full issue #211 parity, and no controls were redesigned.

Baseline worked on: `5465e10` (draft-PR commit) on top of `origin/main` `b5b969d` (v2.19.5).

## Sources of truth (cited)

- Keyboard classic: `src/systems/InputRouter.js:26-42` (`KEYMAP`)
- Keyboard trick layouts: `src/systems/ControlLayouts.js:12-31` (`TRICK_KEYS_RIGHT`, `TRICK_KEYS_LEFT`)
  applied by `src/systems/InputRouter.js:150-155` (`_binding` → `layoutButton`)
- Gamepad: `src/systems/InputRouter.js:52-73` (`GP_BINDINGS`, W3C standard mapping)
- Touch overlay: `src/systems/TouchOverlay.js:35-55` (`TOUCH_CLUSTERS`) and
  `src/systems/TouchOverlay.js:66-71` (`touchButtonFor` swap)
- Pad buttons: `src/systems/VirtualPad.js:18-21` (`HELD_NAMES`); derivation `src/systems/PadDerive.js:16-27`

Run-time evidence: `tests/src/issue-211-input-reachability.test.js` (matrix) and
`tests/src/issue-211-gamepad-alias.test.js` (reproduction). The tests assert reachability through
`VirtualPad`'s real per-button held sets, not by re-reading the tables.

## Reachability table

`mapped` = the input can set that raw pad button / derived pad field. `NOT mapped` = it cannot.
Touch columns are the **Classic** overlay and the **Trick Deck** overlay (Tricks Right/Left share the
same touch swap: `touchButtonFor` treats any non-classic layout as `trickDeck`,
`src/systems/TouchOverlay.js:110-123`).

| Action (pad field) | Tricks Right keyboard | Tricks Left keyboard | Classic keyboard | Touch Classic | Touch Trick Deck | Standard gamepad |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| push | NOT mapped | NOT mapped | `KeyW` → push (`InputRouter.js:27`) | PUSH button (`TouchOverlay.js:45`) | NOT mapped (push→divebomb, `TouchOverlay.js:68`) | RT button 7 value > 0.25 (`InputRouter.js:60,48`) |
| brake | NOT mapped | NOT mapped | `KeyS` → brake (`InputRouter.js:30`) | BRAKE (`TouchOverlay.js:36`) | BRAKE still present (`TouchOverlay.js:36`, pass-through `TouchOverlay.js:70`) | B button 1 (`InputRouter.js:54`) |
| tuck | `KeyD` → tuck (`ControlLayouts.js:20`) | `ArrowRight` → tuck (`ControlLayouts.js:30`) | A+D together (derive, `PadDerive.js:23`) | TUCK (`TouchOverlay.js:37`) | TUCK (`TouchOverlay.js:37`) | LT button 6 value > 0.4 (`InputRouter.js:59,48`) |
| tiltBack | `ArrowDown` (`ControlLayouts.js:14`) | `KeyS` (`ControlLayouts.js:24`) | `KeyA` (`InputRouter.js:28`) | TILT BACK (`TouchOverlay.js:38`) | TILT BACK | D-pad left btn 14 (`InputRouter.js:65`) |
| tiltForward | `ArrowUp` (`ControlLayouts.js:13`) | `KeyW` (`ControlLayouts.js:23`) | `KeyD` (`InputRouter.js:29`) | TILT FWD (`TouchOverlay.js:39`) | TILT FWD | D-pad right btn 15 (`InputRouter.js:66`) |
| heliLeft | NOT mapped | NOT mapped | `ArrowLeft` (`InputRouter.js:34`) | SPIN CCW (`TouchOverlay.js:42`) | NOT mapped (heliLeft→corkscrew, `TouchOverlay.js:69`) | LB btn 4 **and** RS axis2 < −0.5 (`InputRouter.js:57,71`) |
| heliRight | `ArrowRight` (`ControlLayouts.js:15`) | `KeyD` (`ControlLayouts.js:25`) | `ArrowRight` (`InputRouter.js:35`) | SPIN CW (`TouchOverlay.js:44`) | SPIN CW | RB btn 5 **and** RS axis2 > 0.5 (`InputRouter.js:58,72`) |
| airBrake | `KeyA` (`ControlLayouts.js:18`) | `ArrowLeft` (`ControlLayouts.js:28`) | `ArrowUp` (`InputRouter.js:36`) | AIR BRAKE (`TouchOverlay.js:43`) | AIR BRAKE | X btn 2 (`InputRouter.js:55`) |
| parachute | `KeyW` (`ControlLayouts.js:17`) | `ArrowUp` (`ControlLayouts.js:27`) | `ArrowDown` (`InputRouter.js:37`) | CHUTE (`TouchOverlay.js:47`) | CHUTE | Y btn 3 (`InputRouter.js:56`) |
| divebomb | `KeyS` (`ControlLayouts.js:19`) | `ArrowDown` (`ControlLayouts.js:29`) | NOT mapped | NOT mapped (classic overlay has no divebomb) | DIVEBOMB (push→divebomb, `TouchOverlay.js:68`) | **NOT mapped — no gamepad binding** (`GP_BINDINGS`, `InputRouter.js:52-73`) |
| corkscrew | `ArrowLeft` (`ControlLayouts.js:16`) | `KeyA` (`ControlLayouts.js:26`) | NOT mapped | NOT mapped (classic overlay has no corkscrew) | CORKSCREW (heliLeft→corkscrew, `TouchOverlay.js:69`) | **NOT mapped — no gamepad binding** (`GP_BINDINGS`, `InputRouter.js:52-73`) |
| hop | Space (`InputRouter.js:31`) | Space | Space | HOP (`TouchOverlay.js:46`) | HOP | A btn 0 (`InputRouter.js:53`) |
| reset | ShiftLeft/Right (`InputRouter.js:32-33`) | ShiftLeft/Right | ShiftLeft/Right | RESET (`TouchOverlay.js:50`) | RESET | Back btn 8 (`InputRouter.js:61`) |
| pause | Escape (`InputRouter.js:38`) | Escape | Escape | PAUSE (`TouchOverlay.js:51`) | PAUSE | Start btn 9 (`InputRouter.js:62`) |
| confirm (edge) | Space/Enter (`InputRouter.js:31,39`) | Space/Enter | Space/Enter | **NOT mapped** (`confirm` not in TOUCH_CLUSTERS) | NOT mapped | A btn 0 (`InputRouter.js:53`) |
| Menu directions up/down/left/right | — | — | Arrow keys; W/S also emit up/down | — | — | D-pad 12/13 + left stick axes 0/1 (`InputRouter.js:63-70`) |

Note: D-pad left/right (buttons 14/15) are also read directly by `MenuInput._pollPad()` as menu
left/right (`src/ui/MenuInput.js:174-175`), which the per-action columns above do not express.

## Plain findings

- **`divebomb` has no gamepad binding.** `GP_BINDINGS` (`InputRouter.js:52-73`) contains no entry with
  `pad: 'divebomb'`.
- **`corkscrew` has no gamepad binding.** No `GP_BINDINGS` entry sets `pad: 'corkscrew'`. On a gamepad
  the Trick Deck's signature tricks are unreachable; on touch they exist only via the overlay swap.
- Trick Deck keyboard layouts (Tricks Right / Left) intentionally drop `push`, `brake` and `heliLeft`
  (verified: `tests/src/issue-211-input-reachability.test.js`), so Classic and the Trick Deck keyboard
  sets are not interchangeable.
- Touch `confirm` is never mapped: it is an edge-only pad field (`VirtualPad.js:17`) and has no overlay
  button, so touch users confirm via `anyKey`/`hop` paths only.
- **Ground brake default key is undecided (#30).** No ground-brake pad field exists in `HELD_NAMES`
  (`VirtualPad.js:18-21`); this matrix does not invent one.

## Gamepad alias defect (reproduced)

`GP_BINDINGS` binds two physical inputs to one pad button:

| Physical alias | Pad button | Binding |
|---|---|---|
| LB (button 4) | `heliLeft` | `InputRouter.js:57` |
| RSLeft (axis 2 < −0.5) | `heliLeft` | `InputRouter.js:71` |
| RB (button 5) | `heliRight` | `InputRouter.js:58` |
| RSRight (axis 2 > 0.5) | `heliRight` | `InputRouter.js:72` |

Before the fix, `_pollGamepads()` wrote each binding with the shared source id `'gamepad'`
(`VirtualPad.setButton` tracks sources per button, `VirtualPad.js:102-114`). Releasing one alias
removed `'gamepad'` from the button's held set and therefore cancelled the other alias still physically
held.

**Reproduction** (`tests/src/issue-211-gamepad-alias.test.js`, unchanged code) failed:

- `c. releasing LB keeps the still-deflected right stick holding heliLeft` — expected `heli === -1`,
  received `0`.
- `d. releasing the right stick keeps the still-held LB holding heliLeft` — expected `heli === -1`,
  received `0`.

**Fix (minimal, `src/systems/InputRouter.js:289-321`):** `_pollGamepads()` now aggregates all bindings
per target pad button (`padNext`) and writes the pad once per aggregate, still using the single
`'gamepad'` source. `GP_BINDINGS`, the pad public shape, `VirtualPad`'s contract and the emitted
`INPUT_ACTION` `source` (`'gamepad'`) are unchanged. After the fix all alias cases pass.

## Honest limitations

- **Gamepad polling granularity.** Gamepad state is sampled synchronously in `poll()`
  (`src/systems/InputRouter.js:332-342` → `_pollGamepads`, `:289-321`), not from timestamped DOM events. Presses shorter than
  one poll interval, or multiple edges between two polls, are coalesced. No gamepad event timestamps are
  fabricated and none are claimed to have keyboard parity; fair keyboard/touch scheduling is issue #115
  (`tests/determinism/fair-input*.test.js`), and this leaf does not extend it to gamepads.
- This is one bounded leaf. It does **not** claim issue #211 is complete.# Simulation / presentation causal isolation (issue #140)

Status: diagnostic evidence, Team B, 2026-11-21/22, base `b51ab36`, merged with `origin/main` at `14e9c95` (v2.19.0, including #155 and the released Kodiak shoves); integrated for v2.19.1 with the Kodiak shove release v2.19.0. The digest used
here is a **test tool and is non-authoritative**. Replay Contract v1.0 (#152) and the `fingerprintState` of #165 (now on
main) are authoritative. Nothing in `src/` imports the digest.

## Verdict

For a fixed per-tick input tape, the sim's authoritative state was **bit-identical on every tick** under all of
these changes: render cadence (30, 60, 120 and 144 Hz, plus a jittery 4-45 ms schedule), camera zoom, scroll and
shake, particles (off or flooded), audio (muted, absent, no `AudioContext`, every call throwing), viewport size,
aspect ratio and DPR (including resizes mid-run), the HUD scene stopped, pause/resume, and reduced-motion /
screen-shake settings changed mid-run. The authoritative state covers sled compound pose and velocity (all 6
parts), the physics/scramble RNG, Matter world membership **and order**, contact warm-start impulses, terrain
chunks, hazards, pickups, shards, Kodiaks, score, BSOD, crash and timers.

The matrix found three real problems and all three are fixed:

| # | Leak | Effect | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | **Palette / colour-blind toggle mid-run** (Pause > Settings) rebuilt every live terrain collider | Sled pose, Matter world order and contact pairs diverged from the next tick (301 after a toggle at 300) on all 4 fixtures. Kodiak and score state followed | `TerrainMesh.redrawChunk` repaints graphics only; the palette setting uses it |
| L2 | **A throwing audio engine** froze the game | `renderFrame` read `audio.getWorldDanceSample()` unguarded. Phaser's RAF step reschedules only after the frame callback returns, so one throw stopped the loop and the simulation | `WorldDance.readWorldDanceAudio` never throws (warns once); the jukebox/billboard reads in `create` and the track-change handler are guarded too |
| L3 | **Biome-sector entry** repainted through the same collider rebuild as L1 (deterministic, but a repaint feeding physics) | `biome` fixture: a twin with the biome repaint stubbed out diverged at the **entry tick 398** (world order, terrain colliders; contacts from 496) | **Owner-approved physics change**: `refreshPalette` always uses `redrawChunk`; `SIM_REVISION` 2 → 3 (below) |

One known camera read was detected here and fixed by its own issue (#155, now merged):

| # | Read | Effect today | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| K1 | `updateGroundTelegraph` passes `this._view.right` (the rendered camera, one frame stale) to `planTelegraph` | **Only** the `onScreen` flag of telegraph marks differs, and only the renderer reads it. Warn/hop SFX, `teleAtMs`, crash-report arrival and all physics are camera-independent. Seen in 11 matrix cells (zoom, shake, 30 Hz, jitter) | **Fixed by #155** (merged): the sim plans with `planTelegraphMarks` (no camera input); only the renderer adds `onScreen`. `tests/determinism/telegraph-camera-independence.test.js` is now a plain regression test (call site and planner), and the 11 former cue cells are isolated |

## Method

- **Real built game** (`npm run build` + `vite preview`), headless Chromium (SwiftShader WebGL), one fresh page per
  run. `RunScene.update` is held until the scene exists, the loop sleeps, and frames are stepped with
  `game.step(t, dt)`.
- **Per-tick input tape.** The probe installs a tape as `run.tapePlayer` (the ghost-replay hook), so every tick
  sees the same pad whatever the display rate. This separates "render cadence changes how many ticks run per frame"
  (allowed) from "presentation feeds the sim" (a leak). Frame-granular input, which is #115's territory, runs as
  separate `*-polled` cases, report only.
- **Digest after every `simTick`**: `tools/conformance/causal-digest.mjs`. Subsystems fall into three classes:
  - *authoritative*: `sled, rng, world, contacts, terrain, hazards, powerups, shards, kodiaks, score, bsod, crash, timers`;
  - *cue*: gameplay information shown to the player that is not physics: `telegraph, sfx` (scene `playSfx` calls
    inside the tick), `events` (game events emitted inside the tick, wall-clock fields masked), `crashReport`, `glitch`;
  - *cache*: `terrainCache` (generator chunks that cosmetic `heightAt` reads may build early; allowed).
- **Verdicts**: `isolated`, `cue-leak` (only cues differ), `causal-leak` (an authoritative subsystem differs).
  The report gives the first divergent tick and its subsystems, plus a field-level diff at that tick.
- **Positive control** `control-physics-nudge` adds 1e-9 px/step to the sled's velocity at tick 300. It is caught as a
  causal leak at tick 301 on every fixture, at the 1e-13 px level in pose and 1e-10 in velocity. Jest tests pin
  1e-12 sensitivity and world-order sensitivity.

### Fixtures (`FIXTURES` in the probe)

| Fixture | Seed / setup | Exercises | Baseline outcome |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tricks` | `RPLAY59`, scramble on all run, 1200 ticks | hops, helicopter spin, flips, parachute + air brake in the air, tuck; physics/scramble RNG drawn every tick | 555 airborne ticks, score 520 |
| `hazards` | `RPLAY59` from x=50 000, 1200 ticks | biome hazard hit (brace), ground telegraph warn SFX | score 4227 |
| `kodiak` | `BEAR0`, Sync Level 6, 450 m credit | Kodiak pack spawn, telegraph, pass, crash | crashed (hazard) at tick 978, 4 Kodiak events |
| `bsod` | `BSOD140`, wall 260 px behind | BSOD pursuit, wind, catch | caught (`bsod`) at tick 1155 |
| `biome` | `BIOME140@4294967295` (all biome bits), sled 1500 px before the first biome sector boundary (x=30 000) | biome repaint mid-ride, under the sled | enters the biome at tick 398, score 2272 |

Every page runs with `Date` shifted to a fixed day (`FIXED_DATE`, default 2026-11-21T12:00Z; it still advances).
Non-daily runs play *today's* daily rule (`DailyPatch.getDailyInfo()` reads the clock), and without the pin the
`bsod` fixture stopped ending in a catch after midnight UTC. That is a known wall-clock input (Replay Contract v1 C-list,
manifests record `dailyRuleId`), not a presentation leak.

