<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="glow">BITSTREAM BLUFFS</h1>
        <p>Welcome to the digital slopes! Navigate the procedurally generated terrain, perform tricks, and challenge your friends with the same seed.</p>

        <div class="box">
            <h2>OBJECTIVE</h2>
            <p>Ride down the procedurally generated mountain while performing tricks to score points. Avoid obstacles and find the optimal path to maximize your score!</p>
        </div>

        <h2>CONTROLS</h2>
        <div class="box">
            <h3>Tricks Right (default)</h3>
            <p><span class="key">↑</span> Frontflip · <span class="key">↓</span> Backflip · <span class="key">→</span> Helicopter · <span class="key">←</span> Corkscrew</p>
            <p><span class="key">W</span> Parachute · <span class="key">A</span> Airbrake (ground brake) · <span class="key">S</span> Divebomb · <span class="key">D</span> Tuck</p>
            <p><span class="key">SPACE</span> Hop; release early for a shorter ascent.</p>
            <h3>Other layouts</h3>
            <p>Settings → Controls can swap the arrow and WASD clusters (Tricks Left) or select the original Classic layout.</p>
            <p>On a gamepad or touch screen, consult the on-screen control display.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>RIDING</h2>
        <div class="box">
            <p>Use terrain and well-timed jumps to build speed. Landing angle matters; tuck to stay fast, or deploy the sail when airborne.</p>
            <p><strong>Stuck in a valley?</strong> Hop and hold the parachute to catch the wind and regain forward momentum. It does not require a trick combo.</p>
            <p>Wind noise reflects air moving <em>relative to you</em>, not just the sled's speed. Keep an eye on the helmet pom-pom if you cannot hear it.</p>
            <p>Space Mountain has almost no atmosphere: the sail and ordinary wind do not work there, but low gravity gives you more time to maneuver.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>SEEDS</h2>
        <div class="box">
            <p>Each game is generated using a unique seed. Share your seed with friends to challenge them on the exact same terrain!</p>
            <p>You can copy, paste, or manually edit the seed on the start screen.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- 🔽 START: AVALANCHE WARNING SECTION 🔽 -->
        <h2>AVALANCHE WARNING</h2>
        <div class="box">
          <p><strong>⚠️ WARNING: THE BIT STREAM APPROACHES</strong></p>
          <p>Somewhere behind you—beneath the snow, beneath the code—a force is unraveling the mountain.</p>
          <p>No one knows exactly what it is.</p>
          <p>Some riders call it <em>The Bitrot Blizzard</em>—an endless, unraveling corruption gnawing at the terrain.<br>
             Others call it <em>The Bit Stream Of Death</em> (BSOD)—a cold, calculating wave of deleted possibilities.<br>
             And some, with a look in their eyes like they've seen too much, just call it <em>The Snow Crash</em>.</p>
          <p>❄️ It does not slow.<br>
             🧠 It does not forget.<br>
             💾 It does not <em>crash</em>.</p>
          <p>It <strong>terminates</strong>.</p>
          <p>If it catches you, your run ends in corruption—erased from memory, dumped to void.</p>
          <p><strong>🛷 How to survive?</strong><br>
             - Keep moving.<br>
             - Ride like the fate of your file system depends on it.<br>
             - Do your tricks, but <em>don’t linger</em>.<br>
             - Whatever you do, <strong>don’t stop to look back</strong>.</p>
          <p>The BSOD compresses the atmosphere ahead into a tailwind. The faster you move with that air, the quieter it can become—even if the wall is close.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- 🔼 END: AVALANCHE WARNING SECTION 🔼 -->

        <!-- 🔽 START: TERRAIN COLORS SECTION 🔽 -->
        <h2>TERRAIN COLORS</h2>
        <div class="box">
          <p>The slopes of Bitstream Bluffs are streaked with <strong>neon colors</strong>—each with unique effects on your ride:</p>
          <ul style="text-align: left; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <li><span style="color: #00ffff; font-weight: bold;">Blue</span>: <strong>Extra Points!</strong> — Riding over blue terrain gives you a score bonus. Chase these streaks for high scores.</li>
            <li><span style="color: #00ff88; font-weight: bold;">Green</span>: <strong>Speed Boost!</strong> — Green terrain has <em>less friction</em>. You'll accelerate faster and maintain more speed. Great for big jumps and outrunning danger.</li>
            <li><span style="color: #ff00ff; font-weight: bold;">Magenta</span>: <strong>Slows You Down!</strong> — Magenta terrain has <em>more friction</em>. It can sap your momentum, so watch out when speed matters.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Mastering when and how to use each terrain type is key to survival and high scores.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- 🔼 END: TERRAIN COLORS SECTION 🔼 -->

        <h2>TIPS</h2>
        <div class="box">
            <ul style="text-align: left; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
                <li>Build momentum before attempting jumps</li>
                <li>Land on downward slopes to maintain speed</li>
                <li>Chain tricks together for combo multipliers</li>
                <li>Use the seed system to practice difficult sections</li>
                <li>Try to find secret paths and shortcuts in the terrain</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

